{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/cycleBasis()"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A cycle basis: the fundamental cycles of the breadth-first spanning forest, one for each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge outside the forest, in ascending position of that edge, so "},{"code":"edgeCount - vertexCount + c","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cycles for c components. Roots are taken in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order and edges in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order; a vertex’s tree edge is the one that discovered it. Self-loops and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges are supported: a loop is a cycle of its own, and a second copy of an edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closes a cycle of length 2."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cycleBasis","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cycle","identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Cycle","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">]","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every cycle in the basis has exactly one edge outside the forest, so the cycles are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"independent, and every cycle of the graph is a sum of them (mod 2). Each starts at its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"least vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order and leaves it through the lesser of its two edges there.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(n + m) plus the total length of the cycles.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"UndirectedCycles.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cycles\/UndirectedCycles.swift#L72"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6CyclesE10cycleBasisSay5Walks5CycleVy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGGyF","role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Cycles"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cycleBasis","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","text":"Cycle","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">]","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"method","title":"cycleBasis()"},"kind":"symbol","sections"